    "title": "DeSantis names Sterling to FKAA board - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n5 hours ago KEY WEST — Florida Gov. Ron DeSantis has appointed Erica Sterling to the Florida Keys Aqueduct Authority board.\nFKAA is the Keys’ water utility. The governor’s office announced the appointment Nov. 21.\nSterling is a partner at the Key West-based law offices of Spottswood, Spottswood, Spottswood & Sterling PLLC.\nShe serves as a member of the Star of the Sea Foundation board and the Monroe County Bar Association. Sterling earned a bachelor’s degree in accounting, a master’s degree in accounting and a law degree from the University of Florida.",
